# Update

When Jeremy says **update** (or **merge PRs**), that is the whole job:

1. Merge every remaining open PR into `main`.
2. Delete each PR branch after it is on `main`.
3. Delete leftover remote and local `cursor/*` (and any other stale) branches. `main` should be the only branch unless he says otherwise.
4. Bump the cabin release version (patch of `VERSION` / `[workspace.package] version`) and update **all of GitHub** to match: `Cargo.toml`, grokhub rows in `Cargo.lock`, `README.md` latest, shipping specs, `packaging/PKGBUILD`, `packaging/aur/{PKGBUILD,.SRCINFO,grokhub.install}` (`pkgver`, `#tag=v…`, `pkgrel=1`), and version asserts in `cli.rs` / `oauth.rs`. Then tag `vX.Y.Z` and `git push origin vX.Y.Z` so `.github/workflows/release.yml` publishes the GitHub Release. Do not leave GitHub Latest on an older tag (it still showed v2.0.0 after cargo was 2.5.0). Do not bump Imagine `Quality (v2.0)`, specs marked `(do not bump)`, the diagnostics fixture, or `packaging/grokhub.desktop` `Version=` (desktop-entry spec).
5. Update the documents so they match what actually shipped (`README.md`, `/help` / slash text, shipping specs under `docs/`).
6. Leave `main` clean: tests pass, no leftover branches, no stale Electron trees, no draft PR heads sitting around.

Do not leave merged PR heads on the remote. GitHub will not delete them for us (`delete_branch_on_merge` is off). After every merge, `git push origin --delete <branch>` until the repo branch list is only `main`.

If a PR is already superseded on `main` (duplicate cabin work, or an Electron-era branch that would restore deleted `src/` / `desktop/`), record it merged with `git merge -s ours` so the PR closes **without** reverting `main`. Then delete that branch too.

Do not start this pass unless he said **update** (or **merge PRs**). "Don't do it now" means leave PRs and branches alone.
